<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vakil Mosque</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vakil">Vakil</a> Mosque is a mosque in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shiraz">Shiraz</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, built under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karim-khan-zand">Karim Khan</a> during the Zand period, next to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vakil-bazaar">Vakil Bazaar</a>. It is noted for its prayer hall of carved stone columns and its tile decoration. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zand-dynasty">Zand Empire</a> list it among the finest examples of eighteenth-century Persian architecture in the Zand capital.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vakil-mosque.jpg" alt="Vakil Mosque" width="320" height="236" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: dynamosquito from France · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Masdjed-e_Vakil_central_court_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
